  "name": null,
  "problem": "The functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are twice-differentiable on an open interval containing $x=10.$ The values of $f,$ $g,$ and their respective derivatives are given below:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${f}^{″}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{″}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $10$ | $-5$ | $0$ | $3$ | $-20$ | $-2$ | $-6$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to 10}\\frac{f(x)+5}{2x+g(x)}.$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
